.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_EVENT_RETRIEVE_COOKIE 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_event_retrieve_cookie ,
.Nm ndi_event_tag_to_cookie ,
.Nm ndi_event_cookie_to_tag ,
.Nm ndi_event_cookie_to_name ,
.Nm ndi_event_tag_to_name
.Nd look up and translate nexus event cookies
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_event_retrieve_cookie
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t handle"
.Fa "dev_info_t *child_dip"
.Fa "char *eventname"
.Fa "ddi_eventcookie_t *cookiep"
.Fa "uint_t flag"
.Fc
.Ft "ddi_eventcookie_t"
.Fo ndi_event_tag_to_cookie
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t handle"
.Fa "int event_tag"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_event_cookie_to_tag
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t handle"
.Fa "ddi_eventcookie_t cookie"
.Fc
.Ft "char *"
.Fo ndi_event_cookie_to_name
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t handle"
.Fa "ddi_eventcookie_t cookie"
.Fc
.Ft "char *"
.Fo ndi_event_tag_to_name
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t handle"
.Fa "int event_tag"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va handle
Event handle to search.
.It Va child_dip
Child requesting the event cookie.
.It Va eventname
Null-terminated event name.
.It Va cookiep
Output address for an event cookie.
.It Va flag
Zero to permit ancestor lookup, or \fBNDI_EVENT_NOPASS\fP.
.It Va event_tag
Numeric tag assigned by the nexus event definition.
.It Va cookie
Event cookie to translate.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBndi_event_retrieve_cookie()\fP looks up \fBeventname\fP among the events bound to
\fBhandle\fP and returns the cookie in \fB*cookiep\fP.
It is normally used in a nexus driver's \fBbus_get_eventcookie\fP entry point.
If the name is not found and \fBNDI_EVENT_NOPASS\fP is not set, the request is
forwarded to an ancestor using \fBndi_busop_get_eventcookie()\fP.
With \fBNDI_EVENT_NOPASS\fP, a local miss returns failure.
The root nexus must not attempt to forward a request beyond the root.
.Pp
The remaining functions translate between tags, cookies, and names within
the supplied handle only.
They do not search ancestors.
\fBndi_event_tag_to_cookie()\fP finds a cookie by numeric tag.
\fBndi_event_cookie_to_tag()\fP finds the tag of a cookie bound to the handle.
\fBndi_event_cookie_to_name()\fP and \fBndi_event_tag_to_name()\fP return the
definition's name.
.Pp
Cookies and returned names are borrowed references.
Do not modify or free them.
Keep the event definition bound and its storage valid while using them.
An ancestor cookie returned by retrieval is not necessarily bound to the
local handle and may therefore fail a local conversion lookup.
.Sh CONTEXT
Cookie retrieval may be called from user or kernel context.
Local conversion functions may also be used by event callbacks at the
interrupt level for which the handle was initialized.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Retrieval returns \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP for a local match, \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP for
a local miss with \fBNDI_EVENT_NOPASS\fP, or the ancestor bus operation status.
Pointer-valued conversion functions return \fBNULL\fP when no match exists.
\fBndi_event_cookie_to_tag()\fP returns the tag, or \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP for an unknown
cookie.
Choose tags that do not collide with that failure value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_event_alloc_hdl 9F ,
.Xr ndi_post_event 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_definition 9S
